       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-10-20 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>CA-BCCI Umpire Exchange Program Commences</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Australian umpire Ben Treloar and Indian umpire Parashar Joshi are participating in the CA-BCCI Umpire Exchange Program to gain experience in domestic leagues. Treloar will officiate two Ranji Trophy matches, starting with Delhi versus Gujarat from October 18 to 21, followed by Mumbai versus Haryana.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/ca-bcci-umpire-exchange-program-commences.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Parashar Joshi will travel to Australia to officiate two Sheffield Shield matches and one One Day Cup game between Queensland and Tasmania. The exchange is designed to provide exposure to international officiating conditions for both match officials.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the exchange program details and the specific match assignments for both umpires, missing only minor biographical background which is not essential.</p>
