       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-20 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Director Selvaraghavan Rewrites 'Pudhupettai' Script, Sparking Sequel Hopes</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Director Selvaraghavan has announced on Instagram that he is rewriting the story of the 2006 cult film 'Pudhupettai', sparking excitement among fans for a potential sequel. Nearly two decades after its release, the dark crime film remains famous for Dhanush's acclaimed portrayal of Kokki Kumar. While Selvaraghavan has previously hinted at a second installment, concrete details regarding production timelines, cast involvement, and plot specifics remain undisclosed. An official statement and formal announcement regarding the progress of 'Pudhupettai 2' are still pending from the director.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/director-selvaraghavan-rewrites-pudhupettai-script-sparking-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the development regarding the script rewrite and the lack of concrete production details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/tamil/movies/news/will-dhanush-return-as-kokki-kumar-in-pudhupettai-2-selvaraghavan-drops-fresh-hint-about-the-long-awaited-sequel/articleshow/135069337.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
