     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-20 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Secures 22 Medals at Asian Para Games Day 2, Sheetal Devi in Archery Final</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Asian Para Games</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#archery</span> <span>#athletics</span></div>
       <p>India commenced Day 2 of the Asian Para Games in Aichi-Nagoya with a strong performance, pushing its overall medal tally to 22, comprising 5 gold, 8 silver, and 9 bronze medals. This builds on an opening-day haul of 11 medals, which had placed India fourth overall. Deepthi Jeevanji was a standout, securing a gold medal in the women's 400m T20 final and setting a new Games Record of 56.36 seconds.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/india-secures-22-medals-at-asian-para-games-day-2-sheetal-de.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Further success on the track and field saw Pradeep Kumar clinch silver and Ayush Verma secure bronze in the Men's Javelin Throw F53/F54 final, achieving a double podium finish. Kumar recorded a personal best of 27.45m, while Verma's best throw was 17.88m. In shooting, two-time Paralympic medallist Manish Narwal claimed silver in the men's 10m air pistol SH1 final, shooting 233.7 and earning a quota spot for the LA 2028 Paralympics. South Korea's Jo Jeongdu won gold with a Games record of 241.3, while India's Rudransh Khandelwal finished seventh.</p><p>History was made in para powerlifting as Ashok secured India's first-ever medal in the discipline at these Games, earning a silver with a 192kg lift behind China's Yi Zou. In table tennis, Tokyo 2020 medallist Bhavina Patel added a bronze in women's singles Class 4-5. Prachi Pandey secured another bronze in women's singles Class 6, and Baby Sahana claimed India's first-ever medal in the standing category of Para Table Tennis with a bronze in women's singles Class 9, marking the nation's third bronze in table tennis at the Games.</p><p>In archery, Sheetal Devi stormed into the final of the women's compound event, defeating Japan's Aya Shinohara 145-137 in the semi-finals, assuring herself of at least a medal. Swati Chaudhary, the first Indian wheelchair woman archer, also advanced to the women's W1 final, guaranteeing at least a silver after beating South Korea's Lee Eunhee 6-2. Praveen Sharma added a bronze in the men's shot put F11 event with a personal best throw of 13.86m. In badminton, Pramod Bhagat and Nitesh Kumar both reached the semi-finals of the Men's Singles SL3, assuring India of further medals.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Exceptional incorporation of all results, medals, athletes, scores, and records mentioned in the source texts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/othersports/asian-para-games-2026-live-updates-day-2-india-medal-tally-results-aichi-nagoya-live-sheetal-devi-manish-narwal-12207839#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
