     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-20 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India-US Talks Advance on Trade, Energy, Russian Oil Amid Rubio Visit</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India-US</span> <span>#trade</span> <span>#energy</span> <span>#diplomacy</span></div>
       <p>Discussions between India and the United States have progressed on key bilateral matters, including trade, investments, and energy ties. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio visited India, holding high-level talks with External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar in Mumbai, also attended by Foreign Secretary Vikram Misri and US Ambassador Sergio Gor.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/india-us-talks-advance-on-trade-energy-russian-oil-amid-rubi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Central to these talks were India's purchases of Russian oil and plans for an oil refinery setup in Texas. The dialogue addressed India's strategic autonomy in decision-making, particularly concerning its diplomatic ties with Russia amidst evolving Western perspectives. The US is actively seeking new sources for refined fuel due to domestic shortages and geopolitical tensions in West Asia and Eastern Europe, with American diesel prices climbing above six dollars per gallon.</p><p>India's refining sector, notably Reliance Industries' facility in Jamnagar, has emerged as a key focus for crude processing into diesel, complementing planned collaborations in Texas. Secretary Rubio highlighted India's stature as the world's most populous nation, largest democracy, and an essential partner across commercial, defence, and Quad initiatives. He noted that progress towards an upcoming trade agreement is nearing completion, stating, &quot;I think there's a small number of items left to wrap up, so I think that will happen shortly.&quot;</p><p>Rubio's itinerary included a scheduled visit to Gujarat to inspect the Reliance oil refinery in Jamnagar. Discussions during his visit also involved prominent Indian business leaders to strengthen broader economic and energy cooperation. Furthermore, the talks touched upon the Lindsey Graham sanctions act, agricultural protections, and the impact of upcoming US midterm elections on governance and foreign policy. Rubio also paid tribute at the 26/11 memorial in Mumbai, reaffirming solidarity against terrorism.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive coverage of the bilateral talks, trade agreement progress, energy cooperation, and specific details from the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/india-us-ties-trade-and-russian-oil-under-focus-as-bilateral-talks-progress-ytvd-3021433-2026-10-20?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
