       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-20 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NMC Withdraws 2023 Medical Education Regulations, Cancels Fines</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NMC</span> <span>#medical regulations</span></div>
       <p>The National Medical Commission has withdrawn the 2023 medical education regulations, the source reports. In doing so, it removed the provision for fines of up to Rs 1 crore that could be imposed on colleges, as well as the separate fine ceiling of Rs 5 la that was previously stipulated.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/nmc-withdraws-2023-medical-education-regulations-cancels-fin.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The move eliminates the financial penalties that were part of the earlier regulatory framework, signalling a shift in the commission’s enforcement approach. No further details on replacement measures were provided in the summary.</p><p>What to watch: impact on medical colleges and future regulatory updates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, concise reporting of the provided source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
