     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-20 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Ravi Kishan Portrays Lord Ram in Ayodhya Ki Ramleela</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>BJP MP and actor Ravi Kishan performed as Lord Ram at the Ayodhya Ki Ramleela in New Delhi on October 19. This marked his first time portraying the deity, following childhood roles as Parshuram, Kevat, and Mata Sita.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/ravi-kishan-portrays-lord-ram-in-ayodhya-ki-ramleela.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Kishan used the occasion to advocate for spirituality and daily meditation to help the youth overcome difficulties and depression. The actor, who continues to balance his parliamentary duties with film projects, emphasized that his journey from humble beginnings was supported by his faith and commitment to Sanatan traditions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively balances the reporting of the Ramleela performance with Kishan's personal remarks on spirituality and his professional life.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/ravi-kishan-recalls-humble-beginnings-as-he-plays-lord-ram-in-ayodhya-ki-ramleela-i-have-previously-played-parshuram-kevat-and-mata-sita/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
