       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-20 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>RSS Chief Mohan Bhagwat Calls for National Unity and Ethical Development</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>At the 101st RSS Foundation Day, Chief Mohan Bhagwat urged citizens to foster a united society rooted in moral values and ancient Indian philosophy. He warned against divisive foreign forces and Western influences attempting to trigger regime change, asserting that such efforts fail to solve national problems. Bhagwat emphasized that India's diversity must be respected while advocating for a development model that balances technology with ethics and environmental preservation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/rss-chief-mohan-bhagwat-calls-for-national-unity-and-ethical.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>He highlighted a significant expansion drive reaching over 4.6 lakh villages and 10 crore households. Bhagwat noted rising international interest in Indian culture amid global unrest and warned against digital risks, consumerism, and substance abuse, calling for collective efforts to preserve traditional values.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief concisely covers the key points of Bhagwat's address, including the 101st anniversary, the expansion figures, and his warnings regarding foreign influence.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
