     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Mongabay India · 2026-10-20 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Scientists Identify New Seahorse Species from Indian Waters</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#environment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Researchers have discovered a new-to-science seahorse species from Indian waters, resolving the taxonomy of a group misidentified for over a century. Originally described by zoologist Johann Jakob Kaup in 1856 based on Japanese samples, Hippocampus histrix was long thought to be a single, widespread species across the Indo-Pacific. However, a study of specimens collected in 2019 at the Thoothukudi Fisheries Harbour in Tamil Nadu revealed a distinct lineage. Published in Zootaxa, the study established that H. histrix comprises three separate species: H. histrix in the Pacific, H. jayakari in the Arabian region, and the newly described Indian Ocean species, Hippocampus amandavincentae.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/scientists-identify-new-seahorse-species-from-indian-waters.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the taxonomic discovery and the naming of the new species while adhering to the word count.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://india.mongabay.com/2026/10/new-to-science-seahorse-is-one-of-three-long-misidentified-species/" rel="noopener">Mongabay India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-20/scientists-identify-new-seahorse-species-from-indian-waters" data-title="Scientists Identify New Seahorse Species from Indian Waters"><b>Share:</b>
