       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-20 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Villupuram Teacher Promotes Scientific Temper in Rural Students</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Science teacher Maria Joseph has spent two decades at Kangeyanur Panchayat Union Middle School near Villupuram fostering scientific curiosity among rural students. By utilizing tools like Foldscopes and telescopes, Joseph encourages practical learning that extends beyond traditional textbooks into experimental science and astronomy.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-20/villupuram-teacher-promotes-scientific-temper-in-rural-stude.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>These efforts have led to significant academic achievements, with over 20 students selected for the national-level INSPIRE science event since 2011. Students have also participated in the Indian Science Congress and conducted research on local environmental issues, such as the impact of brick kilns on agricultural land, through the Children’s Science Congress.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and provides a concise summary of the teacher's accomplishments as detailed in the source.</p>
